1
00:00:06,000 --> 00:00:08,000
[folk music playing]

2
00:00:13,000 --> 00:00:14,000
[guns cocking]

3
00:00:15,000 --> 00:00:17,000
[music continues playing]

4
00:00:18,000 --> 00:00:19,000
[laughs]

5
00:00:33,000 --> 00:00:36,000
[Diego] What? Intruders? Get rid of them.

6
00:00:36,000 --> 00:00:42,000
I'm far too busy at the moment,
so don't bother me with pointless reports.

7
00:00:47,000 --> 00:00:49,000
[opening theme music playing]

8
00:00:52,000 --> 00:00:54,000
[singer singing in Japanese]

9
00:01:48,000 --> 00:01:49,000
[singer singing in English]

10
00:01:50,000 --> 00:01:52,000
[singer singing in Japanese]

11
00:02:11,000 --> 00:02:13,000
DATE X WITH X PALM

12
00:02:36,000 --> 00:02:39,000
-…you've earned a painful demise.
-[bones cracking]

13
00:02:53,000 --> 00:02:56,000
And it's piquing my appetite.

14
00:02:56,000 --> 00:02:57,000
[slashing]

15
00:03:08,000 --> 00:03:09,000
[chuckles]

16
00:03:10,000 --> 00:03:13,000
That's it, the flavor I seek.

17
00:03:16,000 --> 00:03:19,000
Yes! I can feel it.

18
00:03:21,000 --> 00:03:22,000
This is it!

19
00:03:22,000 --> 00:03:23,000
[gasps]

20
00:03:35,000 --> 00:03:39,000
By consuming the aura of the Rares,
he makes it his own.

21
00:03:51,000 --> 00:03:52,000
[muffled laugh]

22
00:03:56,000 --> 00:03:57,000
[door bursts open]

23
00:03:58,000 --> 00:04:01,000
Hey! Who are you? Guards!

24
00:04:02,000 --> 00:04:04,000
What do you think you're doing?

25
00:04:04,000 --> 00:04:06,000
[King] He's worthless.

26
00:04:06,000 --> 00:04:08,000
I don't sense anything at all.

27
00:04:08,000 --> 00:04:12,000
Insolent thugs!
Have you any idea who I am?

28
00:04:12,000 --> 00:04:16,000
I am the absolute leader of this era,
a king among kings.

29
00:04:16,000 --> 00:04:19,000
I am Masador Diego!

30
00:04:20,000 --> 00:04:23,000
Someone tell me why this scum
is claiming to be a king.

31
00:04:23,000 --> 00:04:27,000
It seems to me that in the human world,
it's a very common phenomenon.

32
00:04:28,000 --> 00:04:31,000
Humans without intelligence or talent

33
00:04:31,000 --> 00:04:35,000
end up in positions of power
due to heredity or connections.

34
00:04:36,000 --> 00:04:38,000
[King] That defies all logic.

35
00:04:39,000 --> 00:04:43,000
In the hands of an incompetent,
power brings nothing but ruin.

36
00:04:43,000 --> 00:04:45,000
This must be the work of imbeciles.

37
00:04:46,000 --> 00:04:49,000
We must keep humans on a very short leash.

38
00:04:49,000 --> 00:04:54,000
Sire. They can provide you
with quality meat, however,

39
00:04:54,000 --> 00:04:57,000
not to mention the fact
they are a fully self-renewing resource,

40
00:05:01,000 --> 00:05:04,000
as an acceptable food source
for soldiers like us.

41
00:05:05,000 --> 00:05:10,000
[grunts angrily] You'll leave here at once
if you know what's good for you!

42
00:05:15,000 --> 00:05:16,000
[women whimpering]

43
00:05:17,000 --> 00:05:20,000
[Neferpitou] Please,
allow me to take care of this.

44
00:05:20,000 --> 00:05:23,000
He can be used to control the humans.

45
00:05:23,000 --> 00:05:24,000
[King] Do as you like.

46
00:05:25,000 --> 00:05:26,000
[woman] Wait! No!

47
00:05:27,000 --> 00:05:31,000
Please, spare our lives. We beg of you.

48
00:05:34,000 --> 00:05:35,000
[laughs]

49
00:05:35,000 --> 00:05:38,000
These humans are complete idiots.

50
00:05:38,000 --> 00:05:43,000
Now, I want you to think as hard
as those puny brains of yours can manage.

51
00:05:43,000 --> 00:05:46,000
Have you ever spared a pig or a cow

52
00:06:02,000 --> 00:06:05,000
We'll call this place the Meat Orchard,

53
00:06:05,000 --> 00:06:08,000
and we'll use it
as a human processing plant.

54
00:06:08,000 --> 00:06:09,000
[Neferpitou] Sire.

55
00:06:12,000 --> 00:06:14,000
[narrator] After losing
to Knuckle and Shoot,

56
00:06:14,000 --> 00:06:18,000
Gon and Killua return to the inn
where Palm waits.

57
00:06:20,000 --> 00:06:24,000
[Killua] Before I worry about enemies,
I have to protect Gon from Palm.

58
00:06:27,000 --> 00:06:28,000
[creaking]

59
00:07:01,000 --> 00:07:02,000
[both gasping]

60
00:07:03,000 --> 00:07:05,000
[Palm] You promised me.

61
00:07:17,000 --> 00:07:19,000
[grunts] I'm sorry.

62
00:07:19,000 --> 00:07:22,000
[Palm] I have no interest in an apology.

63
00:07:23,000 --> 00:07:27,000
There's no point in having you
stick needles in your eye either.

64
00:07:33,000 --> 00:07:34,000
There is.

65
00:07:35,000 --> 00:07:39,000
You must accomplish
any one task that I set before you.

66
00:07:44,000 --> 00:07:46,000
Go out with me.

67
00:08:07,000 --> 00:08:09,000
This is none of your business.

68
00:08:14,000 --> 00:08:16,000
Just between Gon and me.

69
00:08:16,000 --> 00:08:18,000
Oh, goodness! Mmm!

70
00:08:18,000 --> 00:08:19,000
[giggling]

71
00:08:19,000 --> 00:08:20,000
[Killua shudders]

72
00:08:22,000 --> 00:08:25,000
I'm telling you, man,
you need to stay away from her.

73
00:08:25,000 --> 00:08:28,000
[Palm] And you need to stop interfering!

74
00:08:28,000 --> 00:08:30,000
This is between Gon and me, remember?

75
00:08:30,000 --> 00:08:33,000
[Killua] You just want an excuse
to keep saying that!

76
00:08:33,000 --> 00:08:34,000
[Palm] Oh, shut up!

77
00:08:35,000 --> 00:08:38,000
Gon and I are going on a date,
and that's final.

78
00:08:39,000 --> 00:08:42,000
Besides, there's somewhere
I really want to go.

79
00:08:52,000 --> 00:08:53,000
[gasps]

80
00:08:53,000 --> 00:08:55,000
What are you talking about?

81
00:08:56,000 --> 00:08:58,000
We are going out.

82
00:08:58,000 --> 00:09:00,000
You promised me, didn't you?

83
00:09:00,000 --> 00:09:01,000
Mmm-hmm.

84
00:09:02,000 --> 00:09:04,000
Then why is he tagging along?

85
00:09:04,000 --> 00:09:08,000
And why would we train, anyway?
You must be joking!

86
00:09:08,000 --> 00:09:11,000
We're dating,
and this will be our first date!

87
00:09:14,000 --> 00:09:16,000
Our first date.

88
00:09:16,000 --> 00:09:17,000
[breathing heavily]

89
00:09:19,000 --> 00:09:21,000
But it's not actually a date.

90
00:09:46,000 --> 00:09:48,000
Just wait, and you'll find out tomorrow.

91
00:09:49,000 --> 00:09:50,000
[Palm] Oh.

92
00:09:51,000 --> 00:09:54,000
Well, in that case, all right.

93
00:10:01,000 --> 00:10:03,000
No, it was my fault.

94
00:10:03,000 --> 00:10:06,000
I just wanted to surprise you,
thought it might be fun.

95
00:10:07,000 --> 00:10:10,000
Oh, my goodness! A surprise for me?

96
00:10:10,000 --> 00:10:13,000
-I'm keeping an eye on you. [giggles]
-[Killua shudders]

97
00:10:14,000 --> 00:10:15,000
[Gon] All right. Then let's meet

98
00:10:15,000 --> 00:10:17,000
in front of the bulletin board
at 10:00 a.m. tomorrow.

99
00:10:17,000 --> 00:10:18,000
[Palm] I'll be there.

100
00:10:37,000 --> 00:10:38,000
Hmm?

101
00:10:38,000 --> 00:10:40,000
Have you ever been on a date before?

102
00:10:41,000 --> 00:10:42,000
Sure, plenty of times.

103
00:10:42,000 --> 00:10:43,000
[Killua groans]

104
00:10:43,000 --> 00:10:47,000
Except, most all of them
were with my Aunt Mito.

105
00:10:47,000 --> 00:10:50,000
Oh. Okay, I get it now.

106
00:10:50,000 --> 00:10:52,000
Wait. So does that mean
that there were others?

107
00:10:53,000 --> 00:10:57,000
Yep. Sometimes ships with all-female crews
would stop by whale island,

108
00:10:57,000 --> 00:11:00,000
and some of them would only go out
with guys who were younger than them.

109
00:11:01,000 --> 00:11:04,000
I'd show them around town,
and they'd teach me a bunch of stuff.

110
00:11:06,000 --> 00:11:09,000
[Killua] "Stuff"? Hold on. That means…

111
00:11:10,000 --> 00:11:12,000
He's so experienced.

112
00:11:12,000 --> 00:11:15,000
[chuckles] They call women like that
"cougars." Isn't that crazy?

113
00:11:17,000 --> 00:11:19,000
Haven't you ever been on a date, Killua?

114
00:11:32,000 --> 00:11:34,000
And I thought we would stay together.

115
00:11:43,000 --> 00:11:45,000
I've already made up my mind.

116
00:11:47,000 --> 00:11:48,000
[cell phone ringing]

117
00:11:55,000 --> 00:11:56,000
Yeah? Hello.

118
00:11:56,000 --> 00:11:57,000
[Knuckle] It's Knuckle.

119
00:11:59,000 --> 00:12:01,000
-We've located and secured Kite.
-[gasps]

120
00:12:02,000 --> 00:12:05,000
Really? So Kite is okay, then?

121
00:12:15,000 --> 00:12:19,000
so I'd like to tell you he's okay,
but I can't.

122
00:12:19,000 --> 00:12:23,000
Don't worry. I'm sure
there's some way we can bring him back.

123
00:12:23,000 --> 00:12:27,000
[Knuckle] All right. It'll take three days
for us to reach your location.

124
00:12:27,000 --> 00:12:31,000
In the meantime,
be on the lookout for any soldier Ants.

125
00:12:42,000 --> 00:12:44,000
All right!

126
00:12:44,000 --> 00:12:47,000
I knew that Kite was still alive!

127
00:12:47,000 --> 00:12:48,000
[Killua] That's great.

128
00:13:02,000 --> 00:13:03,000
[people gasping]

129
00:13:04,000 --> 00:13:05,000
[humming continues]

130
00:13:07,000 --> 00:13:08,000
Oh, wow!

131
00:13:09,000 --> 00:13:10,000
Look over here!

132
00:13:11,000 --> 00:13:12,000
[stops humming]

133
00:13:13,000 --> 00:13:14,000
[laughs]

134
00:13:14,000 --> 00:13:16,000
[Cheetu] I've found new feeding grounds.

135
00:13:16,000 --> 00:13:17,000
[slurps]

136
00:13:17,000 --> 00:13:18,000
[water flowing]

137
00:13:18,000 --> 00:13:19,000
[Gon] Found it!

138
00:13:19,000 --> 00:13:21,000
Okay, but what's it for?

139
00:13:46,000 --> 00:13:49,000
[Killua] If we run into any soldier Ants
here in the mountains,

140
00:13:49,000 --> 00:13:51,000
we'll be in serious trouble.

141
00:13:52,000 --> 00:13:55,000
On the other hand, if we stay in town,

142
00:14:03,000 --> 00:14:06,000
After all, Gon can't use Nen right now.

143
00:14:09,000 --> 00:14:10,000
So I've gotta protect him,

144
00:14:10,000 --> 00:14:13,000
even if it means
sacrificing everything else.

145
00:14:15,000 --> 00:14:16,000
-[brush rustles]
-[gasps]

146
00:14:27,000 --> 00:14:28,000
Let's hurry up.

147
00:14:29,000 --> 00:14:31,000
[sirens wailing]

148
00:14:34,000 --> 00:14:35,000
[tires screeching]

149
00:14:59,000 --> 00:15:01,000
-Ready.
-And fire!

150
00:15:01,000 --> 00:15:02,000
[gunshots]

151
00:15:10,000 --> 00:15:11,000
He disappeared.

152
00:15:12,000 --> 00:15:13,000
[groaning]

153
00:15:14,000 --> 00:15:15,000
[officers screaming]

154
00:15:25,000 --> 00:15:26,000
You'd think they'd be faster.

155
00:15:27,000 --> 00:15:28,000
This is no fun.

156
00:15:32,000 --> 00:15:35,000
And in other news, at around noon today,

157
00:15:35,000 --> 00:15:39,000
an unidentified creature killed
seven people in the suburbs of Pata.

158
00:15:46,000 --> 00:15:47,000
According to the authorities,

159
00:15:47,000 --> 00:15:51,000
the creature moved faster
than 200 kilometers per hour.

160
00:16:05,000 --> 00:16:07,000
Another city's between us,

161
00:16:07,000 --> 00:16:09,000
with the Miera Mountains
on the opposite side.

162
00:16:10,000 --> 00:16:11,000
We should be okay.

163
00:16:13,000 --> 00:16:15,000
The government has submitted
a capture request

164
00:16:15,000 --> 00:16:17,000
with the Hunter Association.

165
00:16:25,000 --> 00:16:28,000
[Gon] I guess tomorrow
we'll both be on our own, huh?

166
00:16:28,000 --> 00:16:31,000
[Killua] Yeah. I'll be training at the gym
pretty much the whole day.

167
00:16:36,000 --> 00:16:37,000
[Killua] Yeah, right.

168
00:16:38,000 --> 00:16:41,000
I can't just leave Gon alone
when he's vulnerable.

169
00:16:46,000 --> 00:16:48,000
-[Palm] Gon, over here.
-Huh?

170
00:17:03,000 --> 00:17:05,000
I didn't even recognize you.

171
00:17:06,000 --> 00:17:07,000
[Killua] Who are you?

172
00:17:08,000 --> 00:17:10,000
Do I look strange to you?

173
00:17:10,000 --> 00:17:13,000
Mmm-mmm. You look really pretty.

174
00:17:13,000 --> 00:17:16,000
Oh, no, please stop it.
You're being far too loud.

175
00:17:25,000 --> 00:17:26,000
[Killua groans]

176
00:17:46,000 --> 00:17:49,000
[Killua] Damn it!
What the hell am I doing here?

177
00:17:58,000 --> 00:18:01,000
There's no telling
when the enemy might show up.

178
00:18:48,000 --> 00:18:51,000
Either way, I'll probably run into it.

179
00:18:53,000 --> 00:18:54,000
Should I warn them?

180
00:19:09,000 --> 00:19:10,000
It's so pretty.

181
00:19:11,000 --> 00:19:15,000
[Killua] No. If I told them now,
it wouldn't help anyway.

182
00:19:16,000 --> 00:19:20,000
Besides, Gon can't use his Nen right now.

183
00:19:20,000 --> 00:19:23,000
If he gets all upset about Kite
and flies off the handle,

184
00:19:23,000 --> 00:19:24,000
then he's done for.

185
00:19:26,000 --> 00:19:28,000
And knowing Palm,

186
00:19:28,000 --> 00:19:31,000
she'll go 100% nuts
if I interrupt her date.

187
00:19:32,000 --> 00:19:34,000
If she breaks the silence
with her screaming,

188
00:19:35,000 --> 00:19:37,000
any Ants that are nearby
will notice us for sure.

189
00:19:37,000 --> 00:19:39,000
[Palm] Thanks, but I'm fine.

190
00:19:39,000 --> 00:19:40,000
[giggles]

191
00:19:40,000 --> 00:19:41,000
[Gon chuckles]

192
00:19:42,000 --> 00:19:43,000
[Killua] I can't let them know.

193
00:19:48,000 --> 00:19:49,000
[imperceptible]

194
00:19:57,000 --> 00:19:59,000
I'll handle this myself.

195
00:20:14,000 --> 00:20:15,000
[gasps]

196
00:20:43,000 --> 00:20:48,000
[Rammot] Ah! I thought I smelled a human.

197
00:20:48,000 --> 00:20:50,000
[gasps] It's him.

198
00:20:59,000 --> 00:21:01,000
It looks like your luck's run out, kid.

199
00:21:06,000 --> 00:21:09,000
Of course, it won't last forever,
you know.

200
00:21:35,000 --> 00:21:38,000
It doesn't matter if you talk or not,
I suppose.

201
00:21:51,000 --> 00:21:52,000
[Killua] He's right.

202
00:22:02,000 --> 00:22:06,000
I've gotta protect Gon,
no matter what it takes.

203
00:22:11,000 --> 00:22:13,000
[closing theme music playing]

204
00:22:22,000 --> 00:22:24,000
[singer singing in Japanese]

205
00:23:31,000 --> 00:23:32,000
[upbeat music playing]

206
00:23:34,000 --> 00:23:36,000
[Gon] Next time, "Friend and Journey."

207
00:23:37,000 --> 00:23:39,000
Going back to Whale Island with Killua.

208
00:23:39,000 --> 00:23:41,000
[Killua] Stargazing with Gon.

209
00:23:41,000 --> 00:23:43,000
[both] We're going on a journey!

210
00:23:46,000 --> 00:23:48,000
[singer singing in Japanese]
